# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to something you actually source, e.g.:
#     cp .env.example .env
# then fill in your own values and load it before running:
#     set -a; source .env; set +a
#     python Academic_Researcher.py
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL in the sense that the program will start without
# it — but the email addresses matter a lot in practice (see below).
#
# .env is listed in .gitignore, so your real values will not be committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- Ollama connection -----------------------------------------------------
# Where your Ollama server is listening. Leave unset for a local install.
#   Local:     http://localhost:11434
#   LAN box:   http://192.168.1.50:11434
#   VPN host:  http://your-host.your-tailnet.ts.net:11434
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL="http://localhost:11434"

# The exact model tag to use. Run `ollama list` to see what you have pulled.
# OLLAMA_MODEL="qwen3.5:35b"


# --- Contact email for the free academic APIs ------------------------------
# OpenAlex, Unpaywall and Crossref ask you to identify yourself with a contact
# address. Any real address you own is fine — it does NOT have to be an
# academic one. Unpaywall will REJECT requests using an example.com address,
# which disables one of the main full-text discovery routes, so set this.
OPENALEX_EMAIL="your.email@example.com"
UNPAYWALL_EMAIL="your.email@example.com"
CROSSREF_EMAIL="your.email@example.com"


# --- Optional API keys -----------------------------------------------------
# Both are free and both are genuinely optional.
#
# Semantic Scholar: without a key you are heavily rate-limited and the program
# will disable this source after repeated 429 responses. That is expected
# behaviour, not a bug — the other five sources carry the search.
#   Request a key: https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api
# SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY=""

# CORE: without a key this source is skipped entirely.
#   Register: https://core.ac.uk/services/api
# CORE_API_KEY=""
